# Pick reason table

Whenever you recommend a bet (side, total, or parlay leg), put the pick header, then this table. One table per pick. No prose list instead of the table.

```
**Away @ Home Play (odds)** — kick if relevant

| # | Reason |
| --- | --- |
| 1 | Model **X vs posted Y** (gap ±Z). P a vs S b. Alignment c. |
| 2 | Off/def matchup with the actual unit ratings (off vs opp def). Scoring or stop units, not vibes. |
| 3 | Market move and/or why this number instead of the other side (spread vs total, opened vs current). |
```

Row 1 is always model vs the posted number, P/S, alignment.
Row 2 is always the on-field rating mismatch that produces that projection.
Row 3 is always the market structure (open/current, which side failed alignment, key number).

Do not use head-coach / identity / "explosion" as one of the three rows unless that *is* the off/def or market fact. Continuity is already inside the nets.

Parlays: each leg gets this table, or a single table with one row-group per leg. Do not invent new parlay-only reasons.